From bb2458b211b66c944f9f0c63aac38417cda931dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andre Brassfield <andre@brassfield.ai>
Date: Wed, 3 Jun 2026 09:29:47 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 02/11] feat(cron): add until_done work-based loop primitive
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Band 2 of the dynamic-workflow gap plan. Adds a new schedule kind
"until_done" that re-queues the job until a user-defined completion
check returns true, replacing fragile time-based crons with work-based
loops. The completion check is a pure function over external state
(kanban by default; filesystem, etc. extensible) — no LLM in the
control loop, no schema changes to ~/.hermes/kanban.db.

Grammar (parse_schedule):
  until_done:kanban_idle                      — no open tasks anywhere
  until_done:kanban_idle:workspace=NAME       — same, scoped
  until_done:kanban_empty:workspace=NAME      — zero tasks in scope
  until_done:kanban_done:id=t_xxx             — single task terminal
  until_done:kanban_done:workspace=NAME       — all tasks in scope terminal
  until_done:files_match:glob=*,mtime_gt=N    — file freshness check
  until_done:always_done                      — debug helper

Changes:
  - cron/until_done.py (new): criteria parser, 5 checkers, dispatch
  - cron/jobs.py: parse_schedule accepts until_done: prefix, validates
    criteria eagerly at create time
  - cron/jobs.py: compute_next_run returns None when criteria is met,
    re-queues with a 60s poll when not
  - cron/jobs.py: mark_job_run implements the decision tree — done,
    re-queue, or stuck. _until_done_attempts counter + 1440-attempt
    safety cap (~24h of polling) prevents infinite loops on
    unachievable criteria

Tests: 13 unit tests + 1 live test against real jobs.json and real
kanban.db. Both re-queue and completion paths verified; test artifacts
cleaned up after live run.

Safety: this is a fault-isolation improvement, not a security boundary.
Per SECURITY.md §2.2 the only security boundary against an adversarial
LLM is the OS; the completion check is a heuristic over structured
state. Documented in cron/until_done.py.

Part of the dynamic-workflow gap plan:
